In article <3s9sc3$n7i@jac.zko.dec.com>, lionel@quark.enet.dec.com (Steve Lionel) writes:
=
=In article <3s8fqm$6b7@gondor.sdsu.edu>, jernigan@mail.sdsu.edu 
=(Wayne J. Jernigan) writes:
=|>      diff  idwire.xls [users.todd.cdr.ed02.id]idwire.xls
=|>      %DIFF-F-READERR, error reading IDWIRE.XLS;1
=|>      -RMS-W-RTB, 549 byte record too large for user's buffer
=|>
=|>Again, how (and with what utility) do I alter the user buffer in order
=|>to allow for a file of this size to be "compared"?  Yes, I have SYSTEM
=|>privileges.
=
=You can't.  The buffer size is hardcoded in the DIFFERENCES utility code.
=I suspect the maximum size is 512.

Nope.  The maximum buffer size (32767) is hard-coded into RMS.  DIFF allocates
a buffer based on the longest-record-length field in the file header (well,
DIFF's apparently got a default buffer size, and will use that if the LRL is
smaller), and will gladly handle records of up to 32767 bytes, if the LRL field
is set correctly.  Consider the following:

$	SET NOON
$	IF F$SEARCH("TEST.FIX") .NES. "" THEN DELETE TEST.FIX;*
$	CONVERT/FDL=SYS$INPUT:/PAD="*" SYS$INPUT: TEST.FIX
REC
	FORM	FIX
	SIZE	32767
*
$	IF F$SEARCH("TEST.VAR") .NES. "" THEN DELETE TEST.VAR;*
$	CONVERT/FDL=SYS$INPUT: TEST.FIX TEST.VAR
REC
	FORM	VAR
	CARR	CARR
$	DELETE TEST.FIX;
$	COPY TEST.VAR;1 ;2
$	DUMP/HEAD/BLOCK=COUNT=0 TEST.VAR;*

